WEBVTT

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:14.950
<i>Shigeno is the one who's brought the Bats this far, there's no doubt!</i>

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.770
<i>That I can be here today is all his doing.</i>

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.130
<i>I can't let Shigeno...</i>

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.330
<i>end up as a losing pitcher...</i>

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:28.840
<i>in this last game!</i>

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:41.750
Play!

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:43.990
<i>Thanks, old man.</i>

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.210
<i>With your great hit,</i>

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.020
<i>as long as I don't screw up,</i>

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.350
<i>we won't lose this game!</i>

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:56.450
<i>Come, Shigeno!</i>

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:57.870
<i>Here I go!</i>

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.050
Out!

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.300
Yeah!

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.960
It's going to extra innings!

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:25.160
All right!

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.700
We're powerful enough to do this!

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.560
Let's finish it this inning!

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:37.320
Out!

00:01:38.930 --> 00:01:40.400
I can't let you have...

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:42.250
any more points!

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:46.910
Now hitting, number 56: Goro Shigeno!

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:51.920
Ball!

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.230
<i>That Wilkinson...</i>

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.540
<i>He can't pitch more than two innings or thirty pitches.</i>

00:01:57.540 --> 00:01:59.340
<i>He's a typical closer.</i>

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:02.640
Strike!

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:09.190
<i>Their other relief pitchers are worse than him.</i>

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:10.650
<i>In that case...</i>

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:14.360
Foul!

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.900
<i>I'll make him pitch as many balls as I can,</i>

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.030
<i>and get him off the mound...</i>

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:22.700
<i>so that our batters can win this!</i>

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.370
Foul!

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.120
Foul!

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.030
Ball!

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:32.590
He's persistent.

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:33.730
He's...

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.340
He's trying to wear the pitcher down, huh?

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.420
Damn it,

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.680
stop messing with me!

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:42.850
Ball!

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.350
Ball three!

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:45.720
Good!

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.710
If Shigeno gets on base from a walk,

00:02:47.710 --> 00:02:49.600
then next up are our strongest batters!

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:51.010
<i>Don't bat so persistently...</i>

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:52.560
<i>when you're just a pitcher!</i>

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.480
<i>Hurry up and strike out!</i>

00:02:58.740 --> 00:02:59.780
Oh, no!

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.250
The ball just keeps going and going!

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.750
Will it be enough? Will it!?

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.000
Go...

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:10.710
Go.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:13.130
Go!

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:13.130
Tom-san!

00:03:19.070 --> 00:03:20.380
I-It went out!

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.460
H-Home run!

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:23.800
Unbelievable!

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:28.470
It went out!

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.090
They did it!

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:36.360
It's a comeback!

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.770
It seems that the curtain will fall soon.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:50.870
Out!

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.250
Out!

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:06.260
<i>He's really something.</i>

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:14.310
<i>You've earned us a valuable point that can turn this around.</i>

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.230
<i>With that kind of work, we'll shut them out this inning...</i>

00:04:17.670 --> 00:04:20.480
<i>...and we'll win the championship!</i>

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:24.580
Just make sure you get on base,

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:25.320
Wayne!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.660
<i>Let's do it, Shigeno!</i>

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:37.960
Out!

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.630
Pinch hitter, Morita!

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.510
Strike out!

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:49.020
Yes!

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:50.390
Just one more!

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.920
Just... Just one more and then...

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.190
...they... they will win the championship!

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:57.270
Do your best!

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.610
The Falcons are cornered!

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.660
Can the Bats shut them out this inning...

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.620
and win the league championship!?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.490
My dearest wish is so close to being fulfilled!

00:05:13.490 --> 00:05:15.910
T-They'll win, won't they?

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.220
Now, the Falcons...

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.380
are back to the top of their batting order.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.340
Now hitting, number 12: Morrow!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.190
<i>So after all, you didn't throw that 100 mph pitch...</i>

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:35.160
<i>and just quit while you were ahead.</i>

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.980
<i>If I'd known this would be such a bad game...</i>

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:40.830
<i>I wouldn't have come back!</i>

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:47.940
<i>I wasn't able to show you my 100 mph pitch,</i>

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:49.420
<i>but now...</i>

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.320
<i>I'll be able to challenge the Majors and fight you without hesitation next year!</i>

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:03.420
No way!

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.860
All right!

00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.370
Hit! It's a hit!

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.470
The Falcons aren't giving up!

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:12.470
So it won't be that easy after all...

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.310
They've got two outs and a runner on first!

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.690
Now hitting, number 8: Davenport!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:20.460
Damn!

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.920
<i>That was a bad pitch.</i>

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.570
<i>Was he too eager to finish the game?</i>

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.950
<i>He's up next...</i>

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:41.130
<i>I can't let you get your turn!</i>

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.090
Ball!

00:06:46.890 --> 00:06:50.010
His speed and control are dropping.

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.050
It's not surprising.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.340
Not only has he been pitching in every game this series,

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:56.140
but this is now his sixth straight inning!

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:57.850
Just one more!

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.690
Do your best, Shigeno!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:01.930
<i>Let me have my chance.</i>

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:05.480
<i>This time I'll settle the score!</i>

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.690
God damn it!

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:18.410
They've got two outs and runners on first and second this late!

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:27.960
Now hitting, number 1: Joe Gibson Jr!

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.540
Just as I thought.

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:35.810
The god of baseball isn't kind enough...

00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.640
to let you run away this time.

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:45.230
Play!

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.180
A-At this crucial time, <i>he's</i> the batter!?

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.700
Oh, God...

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:55.900
<i>If he hits it, we'll be tied.</i>

00:07:56.660 --> 00:07:59.500
<i>If he hits a long drive, it's goodbye comeback!</i>

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:00.910
<i>Come on!</i>

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:13.040
Foul!

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.030
He's going to walk him!?

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:38.870
T-Time!

00:08:40.520 --> 00:08:43.010
<i>This time you're just giving up?</i>

00:08:44.770 --> 00:08:47.350
<i>What the hell was that 100 mph pitch,</i>

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.960
<i>Honda Jr!?</i>

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:51.720
You're kidding, right?

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.300
What do you think loading the bases will do?

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:56.300
Then they'll just need a single to end our comeback!

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:02.520
I know what you're thinking.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:05.430
Still, you're telling me that...

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.730
the risk is lower than facing Junior straight on?

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:14.700
In that case, let him hit!

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:19.310
If we lose because Junior hits your pitch, it can't be helped,

00:09:19.310 --> 00:09:19.780
but...

00:09:20.380 --> 00:09:23.700
if we walk him and they still win,

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.230
the devastation will be too great!

00:09:25.230 --> 00:09:26.460
What are you saying!?

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:29.570
If we get just one more out we'll win the championship!

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:32.310
When we're in a situation where all we want is for Junior to fail,

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.430
you think I can take a risk where we'll have no chance of winning!?

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:38.340
What did you come all this way to do here?

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:44.430
How can you ever succeed in the Majors if you run away here!?

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:47.690
That's right.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.980
Of course, winning the championship is important...

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:53.970
...but more important than that,

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:56.650
is not giving up.

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:59.490
We've learned that this year,

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:02.110
thanks to you.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:05.950
Fight him head on, Shigeno!

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:07.680
Take him down, then...

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.580
hurry and move up!

00:10:10.950 --> 00:10:13.590
It's only a Minor League championship, after all.

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:18.300
If you're this timid when you get to the Majors, you'll just walk everyone!

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:27.650
After all, the Bats are just idiots.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:29.560
"Just idiots" is just fine!

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.990
H-He sat down!

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>It's on, huh!?</i>

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:56.410
This is a free fansub.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:56.410
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:18.140
If the Falcons get a hit, they'll be tied.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.530
If they hit a long drive, they'll have a farewell comeback.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:22.950
If the Bats can suppress the Falcons, they'll win the championship! It's a decisive battle!

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.530
<i>Come on, Shigeno!</i>

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:28.740
Ball!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.210
<i>His speed increased!</i>

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:38.630
<i>Impossible. He was barely throwing 90 mph a minute ago!</i>

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.220
Ball!

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:42.300
Ball two!

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:44.980
What?

00:11:44.980 --> 00:11:47.340
So he's still planning to walk him?

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:48.900
I-I dunno...

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:52.230
But his pitches' power is completely different from a minute ago.

00:11:52.950 --> 00:11:54.650
Shigeno!

00:11:54.650 --> 00:11:56.730
Take a deep breath!

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:58.400
Use the entire power of your shoulders!

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.860
Don't worry about the runners!

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:11.480
<i>I concentrated so much on trying to show off my growth to Gibson...</i>

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:13.710
<i>that I didn't concentrate enough down here!</i>

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.130
<i>I overworked myself somehow.</i>

00:12:19.660 --> 00:12:23.470
<i>Showing a 100 mph pitch isn't proof of growth.</i>

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:24.390
<i>What!?</i>

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.090
Wind up!?

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.550
When there are runners on!?

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:28.730
Idiot!

00:12:28.730 --> 00:12:30.680
<i>The proof of my growth...</i>

00:12:30.680 --> 00:12:31.930
<i>is the baseball spirit...</i>

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:35.810
<i>I inherited from my dad, which keeps me fearless even in a pinch!</i>

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:38.440
Strike!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:45.410
<i>He got desperate.</i>

00:12:45.410 --> 00:12:47.240
W-Why?

00:12:47.240 --> 00:12:49.330
Shigeno, what are you doing!?

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:53.370
Now, even if it's just a normal hit, it'll be goodbye comeback!

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:59.090
Now, really, if he goes down, we all go down.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:00.990
Still,

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:03.120
that's not too bad, right?

00:13:03.120 --> 00:13:04.840
That's right.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:06.440
I'm thankful.

00:13:06.440 --> 00:13:09.680
To think you'd help us with our farewell comeback.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.770
I only helped prepare your strikeout.

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:30.990
Foul!

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:32.410
Foul!

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.570
99 mph!

00:13:37.570 --> 00:13:39.420
All right! It's finally here!

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:42.840
But he could cut off that ball easily...

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:52.430
<i>I've been waiting for that, Honda Jr!</i>

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.100
<i>This time I'll settle the score for real!</i>

00:13:59.850 --> 00:14:00.770
Foul!

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:08.530
100 mph!

00:14:08.530 --> 00:14:10.700
It's the first in the hundreds since the first game!

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.620
It's still getting faster this far into the game!?

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:21.120
<i>This...</i>

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:22.870
<i>This is it!</i>

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.170
<i>I came back...</i>

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:27.130
<i>to hit that pitch!</i>

00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.100
Foul!

00:14:35.340 --> 00:14:36.970
<i>I see!</i>

00:14:36.970 --> 00:14:39.190
<i>So that's how it was!</i>

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.820
<i>The more trouble you're in, the greater your power becomes!</i>

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.530
<i>You're a clutch pitcher!</i>

00:14:52.610 --> 00:14:57.790
<i>Whether you realize it or not, you will undoubtedly push each other to your limits.</i>

00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:00.170
<i>That's what...</i>

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.670
<i>true rivals do.</i>

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.650
Foul!

00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:17.370
He's keeping up!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.100
They're both monsters!

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.700
<i>Go, you two, and open a new age.</i>

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:24.520
<i>However,</i>

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:28.140
<i>I won't easily give up my seat either.</i>

00:15:29.370 --> 00:15:31.030
<i>I'm awestruck.</i>

00:15:31.030 --> 00:15:34.030
<i>They really live up to the Major name.</i>

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:39.460
<i>These two can see a world one step higher, that we normal people can't see.</i>

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:42.150
<i>Most likely, if things go well,</i>

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:42.920
<i>you'll never...</i>

00:15:43.310 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>have to come back to the Minors again!</i>

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:50.130
<i>It's been fun,</i>

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:52.050
<i>Japanese boy.</i>

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:55.260
<i>As a finale, defeat this great slugger,</i>

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:57.260
<i>and make a toast!</i>

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:13.740
<i>I win!</i>

00:16:27.800 --> 00:16:28.920
<i>My bat...</i>

00:16:36.420 --> 00:16:37.720
Out!

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.930
Game over!

00:16:47.110 --> 00:16:48.570
We did it, Shigeno!

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:52.950
They did it!

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.860
Papa did it!

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:01.250
All right!

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:03.740
The Memphis Bats win the championship!

00:17:03.740 --> 00:17:08.630
The Bats win this year's Triple A Championship, 4 games to 3!

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.480
The Bats...

00:17:11.480 --> 00:17:13.280
My Bats won!

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.090
Congratulations!

00:17:22.180 --> 00:17:23.550
We did it!

00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:35.110
W-Wait a minute!

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:37.110
Why?

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:39.830
The coach is me, so why...?

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:43.900
T-Too bad, Mr. Gibson.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.180
What do you mean?

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:49.530
It was an excellent battle.

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:51.130
Gentlemen,

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:52.960
thanks for today.

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.060
Congratulations on the Bats' championship!

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:06.980
Why, you!

00:18:06.980 --> 00:18:09.100
Today we'll drink until we drop!

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:13.680
Kelloge and Shigeno, you're still too young to drink!

00:18:13.680 --> 00:18:14.990
How boring!

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:17.950
Hey!

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:24.130
Shigeno!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:27.870
I-I'm going to the toilet!

00:18:40.540 --> 00:18:42.010
Do you have a minute?

00:18:46.370 --> 00:18:47.280
What is it?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:50.940
Did you come to congratulate me on the championship?

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:55.480
Tell me where your father's grave is.

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:58.880
A bet is a bet.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:01.180
You struck me out.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:04.280
As promised, I'm going to his grave to apologize!

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:06.950
Hurry up and tell me!

00:19:09.430 --> 00:19:11.540
What, is that it?

00:19:11.540 --> 00:19:13.100
How stupid.

00:19:13.100 --> 00:19:13.920
First of all,

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.630
you hit a home run off me too.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.460
We're even.

00:19:17.460 --> 00:19:19.710
That was a running home run!

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:23.510
Plus, that wasn't your best pitch!

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:26.140
I won't recognize that as winning the bet!

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:30.190
Shut up! Stop nagging about who won or lost in the bet.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:33.300
And anyway, apologizing as an obligation...

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:35.710
isn't something that I or my dad would want.

00:19:36.840 --> 00:19:38.370
It's not an obligation.

00:19:40.250 --> 00:19:42.060
When I look at you,

00:19:42.060 --> 00:19:45.580
I can imagine what kind of player your father was.

00:19:46.140 --> 00:19:47.400
Honestly,

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:50.290
I'm sorry that I insulted him in order to get back at you.

00:19:54.550 --> 00:19:55.840
Enough.

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:59.880
I'll tell my dad about you myself.

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.000
I'll tell him that even though you're impolite and irritating,

00:20:03.000 --> 00:20:05.710
even Gibson has a son...

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:07.810
who bets his life on baseball.

00:20:11.760 --> 00:20:14.920
Next time, I'll strike you out in the Majors!

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:17.330
Shut up.

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:18.640
You'll be the one going down.

00:20:19.660 --> 00:20:21.530
Thanks for the...

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:24.110
frantic and well-fought game I got to watch.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.380
Gibson!

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:40.400
<i>I'm looking forward to next year.</i>

00:20:46.180 --> 00:20:47.300
Let's meet in the Majors,

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:49.200
Goro Shigeno!

00:20:53.070 --> 00:20:54.390
Yeah!

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:57.960
Hold onto the neverending dream

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:00.790
in your heart.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.740
Keep running forward

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:08.410
to the vast plains of the diamond.

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.380
With your 100 miles of

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:24.220
passion and conviction,

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:28.930
go and open a new door.

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:34.560
The lonely mound has taught me

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:40.320
that I'm not alone.

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:44.570
I won't give up

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.820
tomorrow to anyone.

00:21:47.250 --> 00:21:49.160
I want to believe

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:52.600
that love exists here.

00:21:52.600 --> 00:21:56.330
Hold onto the neverending dream

00:21:56.330 --> 00:21:59.130
in your heart.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:00.750
Keep running forward

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:07.050
to the vast plains of the diamond.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:13.220
More valuable than any medal...

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:18.230
The number of times I've risen up after falling

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:24.110
is what I boast about.

00:22:39.080 --> 00:22:43.020
Carry out your own life.

00:22:44.800 --> 00:22:49.930
It doesn't matter if you aren't perfect.

00:22:49.930 --> 00:22:53.180
The shining PRIDE...

00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:55.890
Grasp it with your hands.

00:22:56.370 --> 00:22:58.520
Face the headwind

00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:01.560
straight on.

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:05.130
I won't give up

00:23:05.130 --> 00:23:07.570
tomorrow to anyone.

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:09.860
I want to believe

00:23:09.860 --> 00:23:13.370
that love exists here.

00:23:13.370 --> 00:23:16.500
Hold onto the neverending dream

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:19.640
in your heart.

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:21.710
Until I burn out,

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:28.470
I'll live my life with passion, without regret.

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:12.010
All right!

00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:14.470
Finally the Bats have won the championship!

00:24:15.100 --> 00:24:18.390
Just one more step to the stage of my dreams, the Majors, where Gibson awaits!

00:24:18.800 --> 00:24:22.350
I'm so excited about what new opponents are waiting for me there,

00:24:22.840 --> 00:24:24.310
that I can't wait!

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:28.620
Everyone, look forward to my next challenge!
